---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import Type from '../../components/Type.astro';
import { species, url, hasDocumentedSource } from '../../lib/data';
const regions = [...new Set(species.map((s) => s.region))];
---
<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Pokémon', description: 'Every Pokémon in Origin HeartGold: types, abilities, base stats and how to get it.', tableOfContents: false }}>
	<p>The {species.length} species and forms in the game, with the hack's own types, abilities and base stats.
	Pokémon that are only in the game's data files and never appear in normal play (about half of those from Unova onward, Mega forms other than Charizard's, Gigantamax forms) are left out.{' '}
	{species.filter(hasDocumentedSource).length} have a documented source, including verified held-item forms and calendar encounters,
	and {species.filter((s) => s.battleOnly && !hasDocumentedSource(s)).length} more are forms that only appear in battle.
	Calendar entries are marked separately and captures have not all been tested. Entries with no confirmed way to get them (the Unown letters) are hidden by default.</p>
	<p><a href={url('/calendar/')}>Browse calendar encounters</a> · <a href={url('/mechanics/#held-item-forms')}>Held-item transformations</a></p>
	<div class="table-filter" data-table="mon-table">
		<input type="search" placeholder="Search by name, type or ability…" aria-label="Search Pokémon" />
		<select data-key="region" aria-label="Region">
			<option value="">All Pokédex ranges</option>
			{regions.map((r) => <option value={r}>{r}</option>)}
		</select>
		<label><input type="checkbox" data-key="obtainable" data-show-value="no" /> Show Pokémon with no confirmed source</label>
		<span class="filter-count" aria-live="polite"></span>
	</div>
	<table id="mon-table" class="sortable compact">
		<thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Pokémon</th><th>Type</th><th>Abilities</th><th>Hidden</th><th>BST</th></tr></thead>
		<tbody>
			{species.map((s) => (
				<tr data-region={s.region} data-obtainable={hasDocumentedSource(s) || s.battleOnly ? 'yes' : 'no'} hidden={!(hasDocumentedSource(s) || s.battleOnly)}>
					<td>{s.id}</td>
					<td><a href={url(`/pokemon/${s.slug}/`)}>{s.name}</a>{s.game && <span class="sr-only"> {s.game}</span>}</td>
					<td>{s.types.map((t) => <Type type={t} />)}</td>
					<td>{s.abilities.join(' / ')}</td>
					<td>{s.hidden ?? '—'}</td>
					<td>{s.stats.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0)}</td>
				</tr>
			))}
		</tbody>
	</table>
</StarlightPage>
